  "sn55.10:3.3": "The commentary attributes the large number of deaths to a recent plague (_ahivātaroga_, “viper’s breath disease”). This deadly contagion (malaria?) was known to kill off entire families ([pli-tv-kd1:50.1.1]()). According to the commentaries, the same disease once afflicted Vesālī, prompting the teaching of the Ratanasutta ([snp2.1](), [kp6]()). ",
